<title>UK: P&amp;O H1 pre-tax profit rises to 134.7 mln stg.</title>
<headline>P&amp;O H1 pre-tax profit rises to 134.7 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		15.7		   vs 14.1</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 13.5		   vs 13.5</p>
<p> Pretax profit	    134.7		  vs 131.9</p>
<p> Turnover		   3,436.1		vs 3,060.3</p>
<p>NOTE - Shipping and construction group Peninsular and Oriental Plc said its pre-tax profit was 130.2 million stg before a gain of 4.5 million stg on sale of fixed assets.  </p>
<p> Operating result	 228.6		  vs 205.4</p>
<p> Sale of fixed assets   4.5		    vs 5.7</p>
<p> Interest paid	    98.4		   vs 79.2</p>
<p> Tax paid		   33.7		   vs 39.6</p>
<p> Net taxed		  101.0		  vs 92.3</p>
<p> Attributable	     99.0		   vs 89.0</p>
<p> Pay date		   November 15</p>
<p> Div registration date  October 1</p>
<p> Ex-div date		September 23</p>
<p>NOTE - Breakdown of group's operating profit</p>
<p> P&amp;O Cruises		67.5		   vs 48.2</p>
<p> P&amp;O Ferries		0.5		    vs 24.8</p>
<p> P&amp;O Containers	   20.9		   vs 15.3</p>
<p> P&amp;O Bulk Shipping	2.6		    vs 10.3</p>
<p> Bovis Homes		5.9		    vs 3.1</p>
<p> Bovis Construction     6.8		    vs 4.1</p>
<p> Property development   29.3		   vs 4.0</p>
<p> Investment property    46.1		   vs 47.3</p>
<p> Service businesses     15.4		   vs 14.9</p>
<p> P&amp;O Australia	    24.4		   vs 23.2</p>
<p> P&amp;O European Transport 9.2		    vs 10.2</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
